Work in this repository comes from the plan in `{{ index .Caps "record.plans" }}/`, not from
memory or preference. An epic states an outcome; a spec is one deliverable slice of it
with acceptance criteria; a milestone is a checkpoint specs belong to.

Before starting work, run `ilk blueprint next` — it shows what is ready, from the
record rather than from anyone's recollection. If what you are about to do is not in
the plan, either it belongs in a spec first or somebody should say why it does not.

Every spec declares `epic:` and `milestone:` and carries an `## Acceptance criteria`
section. Those are what make "done" a claim somebody else can check rather than an
assertion, and `ilk check` enforces all three.
